                                <DTC ID="DTCC239EA0" OID="514ebf3f-0adf-417f-8a89-a5373498ad4d">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC239EA0</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6528672</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C239EA0</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_294048392">Control Module Processor</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1125509703">This monitoring checks that each task is activated and executed within its designated timeslot.1. Self check mechanism. Every task monitors itself and must be activated exactly once within its expected time slot (detects too often or too seldom activation)2. Watchdog mechanism. Task monitoring is time-shared with the watchdog handler (detection of permanently missing task)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_191075988">1. Runtime problem2. Malfunction of the system timer</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC239DA4" OID="04dc3db9-ca87-450f-bd28-9634629d5321">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC239DA4</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6528420</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C239DA4</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_294048392">Control Module Processor</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1486845611">-</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_701063421">The jitter monitoring works in the way that a monitor process at specific location in the x1 task checks the difference in time between the current and the last point of this process execution against the ideal task cycle time +/- an allowed jitter.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1248298869">NA</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_871807991">The jitter limit of sensitive part (before monitor process) within x1 task is not held (possible cause : higher priority tasks or x1 task itself takes longer time or long running ISRs)</SD>
